  "term": "rabies",
  "definition": "Rabies is a life-threatening viral infection, usually spread to humans through the bite of an infected dog, that first causes general illness such as fever and headache and then affects the central nervous system. In later stages it can lead to sudden behavior changes, followed by paralysis, lethargy, and coma.",
